@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lyra-opaque-ssh-payload
Lyra MUST NOT inspect, format, persist or log SSH command arguments, environment
values, stdin, stdout, stderr or relayed bytes. Proxy stdout MUST contain only
the SSH relay stream. Child process diagnostics MUST never be copied into logs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lyra-closed-diagnostics
Persistent diagnostics MUST use only reviewed event names and fixed or numeric
fields. Arbitrary error text, URLs, hostnames, labels and process arguments MUST
NOT enter diagnostic files or update status.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lyra-current-gateway-key
Every outer Audi SSH connection MUST pin the key returned for its exact current
route by verified HTTPS. Lookup failure MUST prevent connecting; persistent or
automatically accepted host keys MUST NOT substitute for the current key.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] lyra-agent-fenced-execution
The guest agent executor MUST use only the private verified TLS endpoint, report
started before any tool side effect, bound tool output and duration, and stop
executing when its lease or result RPC fails. It MUST NOT persist or log command
arguments, response bodies, transient tool output or credentials. Authorized
managed skill files and bounded installation receipts containing only request
digests, identifiers, content digests, paths and closed outcomes MAY be persisted
under the managed skill root. Those artifacts MUST NOT enter diagnostics.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] lyra-workspace-closed-events
overalls-workspaced MUST emit only closed guest_workspace event names. Repository
URLs, owners, names, refs, nonces and git stdout/stderr MUST NOT enter the
journal or any other diagnostic. Bounded advertised-ref output MAY be parsed
inside the guest; it MUST never enter diagnostics. Other git output is discarded.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] lyra-guest-telemetry-best-effort
Guest tool telemetry MUST be emitted only after the terminal transition is
acknowledged, use fixed metric and span names without command data or user labels,
and fail independently of guest tool execution. Diagnostic network I/O MUST run
on one bounded observer worker; executor admission MUST remain nonblocking even
when the receiver is unavailable or the fixed queue is full. Trace identifiers may be derived
from a one-way hash of the command ID, but the ID itself MUST NOT enter OTLP.
Guest telemetry MUST remain diagnostic and MUST NOT determine outer fleet SLO compliance.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] lyra-hegel-properties
Lyra's Hegel properties (pinned `hegeltest`, explicit case counts) cover:
configuration input validation (hosts, VM identities, origins, hostnames and
SSH identity names); HTTPS control URL, bounded response and exact status
acceptance; SSH configuration remote names, public-key lines and unmanaged-byte
preservation or marker-ambiguity refusal; known-hosts denial precedence, line
preservation and marker refusal; certificate principal patterns; proxy agent
settings and gateway host-key line binding; update digest, artifact path,
downgrade, staging switch/rollback, cooldown and corrupt-stage refusal;
telemetry bounded metric points and fixed trace data; maintenance history and
artifact origin; git identity round-trip and injection refusal; SSH authorize
roster membership, bounded responses, HTTP 200, duplicate identity, offered-key
proof and home-component names; the guest supervisor candidate recovery and
replacement wait; the `overalls open` stage machine; and workspace receiver
vector agreement, hostile URLs, envelope refusal and the receiver state machine.
Native vsock, kernel attestation and platform services are not covered by
properties.
